The built package also carries the components below, under their own licences;
see LICENSING.md for how they combine.

Repository dependencies
-----------------------

gm8-lib <https://github.com/QuentinJanuel/gm8-lib>, GPL-2.0-only, pinned by commit
in Cargo.toml and fetched by cargo. It is built on gm8exe and gml-parser from
OpenGMK <https://github.com/OpenGMK/OpenGMK>, GPL-2.0-only.

gms-lib <https://github.com/QuentinJanuel/gms-lib>, GPL-3.0-only, the gms-lib git
submodule. It brings its own submodules: UndertaleModTool
<https://github.com/UnderminersTeam/UndertaleModTool> (GPL-3.0), through the fork
<https://github.com/QuentinJanuel/UndertaleModTool>, and that one's Underanalyzer
<https://github.com/UnderminersTeam/Underanalyzer> (MPL-2.0), through the fork
<https://github.com/QuentinJanuel/Underanalyzer>.

In the npm package
------------------

dist/gm8/ is gm8patch compiled to WebAssembly from gm8-lib, with gm8-lib's
LICENSE and NOTICE beside it. Besides gm8-lib's own GPL-2.0-only code it links:
  - Http Dll 2.3 by Maarten Baert, a GameMaker extension DLL embedded as data and
    written into every GameMaker 8 game patched with a mod channel. It is a
    separate work under the GNU LGPL; its source and licence are published at
    <https://www.maartenbaert.be/game-maker-dlls/http-dll-2/>.
  - Rust crates from crates.io, each available under the MIT licence (most also
    under Apache-2.0): adler2, byteorder, cfg-if, crc32fast, crossbeam-deque,
    crossbeam-epoch, crossbeam-utils, either, flate2, itoa, memchr, miniz_oxide,
    once_cell, rayon, rayon-core, serde, serde_core, serde_json, simd-adler32,
    wasm-bindgen, zmij. Cargo.lock in gm8-lib pins their versions.

dist/gms/ is gms-lib's AOT-compiled .NET WebAssembly runtime, with gms-lib's
LICENSE and NOTICE beside it. Besides gms-lib (GPL-3.0-only), UndertaleModLib
(GPL-3.0) and Underanalyzer (MPL-2.0; source at the fork above) it contains:
  - the .NET runtime and base class libraries <https://github.com/dotnet/runtime>,
    MIT, including ICU data (Unicode licence);
  - Roslyn, Microsoft.CodeAnalysis <https://github.com/dotnet/roslyn>, MIT;
  - Magick.NET <https://github.com/dlemstra/Magick.NET>, Apache-2.0;
  - SharpZipLib <https://github.com/icsharpcode/SharpZipLib>, MIT.

The JavaScript in dist/ is sculptr's own source, bundled by esbuild; it has no
runtime npm dependencies.
